From 5044570df17c7d062869384caf4c258c3268cc56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:14:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: native Dolby Vision goes on into the mode of
 the next video

A native Dolby Vision file opened while another plays ("next", another file
of a list, another file) at another frame rate changed the display three
times, four with nvidia-drm: the ordinary output restored in the mode of the
first (nvidia-drm turns the head off and on for it), the mode of the second,
and the start of its native output. Its renderer is kept when its pictures
have the same parameters, so the mode comes from UpdateResolution(), where
CModeChangeHold and the restoration joined to the next mode do not reach. When the renderer
is configured again, the output was restored there as well, and the frames
of the second file started the transport in the mode of the first. The next
file of a list, opened after the first ended, changed it twice: the
restoration joined to its mode, then the start of its native output.

The transport is the same for both videos, and its properties stay on the
connector through a change of mode. CDVModeMove decides:
 - a change of mode while native output carries the transport moves into it,
   without a restoration, where the restoration could be joined to it
   (same window, not 3D, on, another mode), the new mode carries the
   transport at a rate the display takes, and a video takes it: the
   renderer that draws natively now, or, while the end of the video before
   waits for a change of mode, the video that opens and that VideoPlayer
   said goes out natively. The mode is selected and the next frame of the
   transport carries it (a modeset allowed), told before it like a held
   change. The output is kept for a video whose renderer is still to come
   for CModeChangeHold::START_MS, after which the ordinary output comes back
   in that mode, in one commit with it.
 - the renderer of the next video, configured while native output keeps the
   output (waiting for a change of mode, or kept for it by a move), takes it
   over when it draws natively in the same output surface: nothing is
   restored, and the GUI is composed into the picture again.
Anything else ends native output as before. A mode that was moved into and
that no frame carried goes with whatever restoration comes, in one commit
(also the joined one, where another change of mode comes first). A frame that carries
the mode and that the driver refuses counts as any refused frame: after them
the ordinary output comes back in the new mode. In a host model of the window
system: one change of the display where there were three or four (a file
over another), two (the next of a list) or seven (renderer configured again,
nvidia-drm), and none for the next file of a list at the same rate.
---
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/DVModeMove.h               |  86 +++++++++++++
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp           |  12 ++
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.h             |   3 +
 .../windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp | 115 +++++++++++++++++-
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.h  |  14 ++-
 5 files changed, 226 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 xbmc/windowing/gbm/DVModeMove.h

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/DVModeMove.h b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/DVModeMove.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9456bd1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/DVModeMove.h
@@ -0,0 +1,86 @@
+/*
+ *  Copyright (C) 2026 Hades
+ *  This file is part of LibreELEC Hades. It is not in Kodi as Team Kodi publishes it.
+ *
+ *  SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
+ *  See LICENSES/README.md for more information.
+ */
+
+#pragma once
+
+namespace KODI
+{
+namespace WINDOWING
+{
+namespace GBM
+{
+
+/*!
+ * \brief Hades: native Dolby Vision output that goes on from one video to the next, instead of
+ *        ending and starting again around the change of mode between them
+ *
+ * A file opened while another plays (the next one of a list, "next", another file), or the next
+ * one of a list after the one before ended, that both go out natively and want another mode, made
+ * three changes of the display, or two: the ordinary output restored in the mode of the first
+ * (with nvidia-drm, turned off and on), the mode of the second, and the start of its native output;
+ * with the restoration joined to that mode, two. The transport is the same for both videos, and
+ * its properties stay on the connector through a change of mode: the next frame of the transport
+ * can carry the mode (a modeset allowed, its MODE_ID), in one commit.
+ *
+ * Moves(): a change of mode while native output has the output moves into it, without a
+ * restoration: the output carries the transport (TransportLive()); the change is one that the
+ * restoration could be joined to (CModeChangeHold::DVRestoreJoins(): atomic, on, same window, not
+ * 3D, another mode); the new mode is a mode of the transport at a rate that the display takes for
+ * native output; and a video takes it: the renderer that draws natively now, or, while the end
+ * of the video before waits for a change of mode (EndDVBridgeAfterVideo()), the video that opens,
+ * which VideoPlayer said goes out natively. Its first transport frame carries the change of mode,
+ * told before it (CHeldModeAnnouncement::Held()).
+ *
+ * HandsOver(): the renderer of the next video is configured while native output still has the
+ * output, waiting for the change of mode after the video before, or kept for the next video by a
+ * move: the output is not restored when that renderer draws natively and keeps the output
+ * surface (the 8-bit buffers of the transport). Its frames go on in the transport.
+ *
+ * Anything else ends native output as before. A frame that carries the mode and that the driver
+ * refuses counts as any refused frame: the ordinary output comes back after them, in the new
+ * mode, in one commit with it.
+ *
+ * This class only decides.
+ */
+class CDVModeMove
+{
+public:
+  struct State
+  {
+    bool captured = false; //!< native output has the output
+    bool transportLive = false; //!< ... and carries the transport
+    bool disabled = false; //!< native output is disabled after a failure
+    bool joins = false; //!< DVModeChangeJoins(): another mode of the window, on, not 3D
+    bool transportMode = false; //!< the new mode carries the transport, at a rate taken
+    bool rendererNative = false; //!< a renderer draws natively now
+    bool endWaits = false; //!< the end of the video before waits for a change of mode
+    bool nativeOpens = false; //!< VideoPlayer told of this change for a native video that opens
+  };
+
+  static bool Moves(const State& s)
+  {
+    return s.captured && s.transportLive && !s.disabled && s.joins && s.transportMode &&
+           ((s.rendererNative && !s.endWaits) || (s.endWaits && s.nativeOpens));
+  }
+
+  //! \param waiting the end of the video before waits for a change of mode, or a move keeps the
+  //!        output for the next video
+  static bool HandsOver(bool captured, bool picture, bool rendererNative, bool keepsSurface,
+                        bool waiting)
+  {
+    return captured && picture && rendererNative && keepsSurface && waiting;
+  }
+
+  //! How long a move keeps the output for a video whose renderer is not configured yet (its first
+  //! picture, decoded): as long as a START hold waits for it (CModeChangeHold::START_MS)
+  static constexpr int WAIT_MS = 3000;
+};
+
+} // namespace GBM
+} // namespace WINDOWING
+} // namespace KODI
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
index df8e2a5..4e29a97 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
@@ -1634,6 +1634,18 @@ bool CWinSystemGbm::OtherTiming(const RESOLUTION_INFO& res) const
          next.vscan != now->vscan || next.flags != now->flags;
 }
 
+bool CWinSystemGbm::DVTransportModeOf(const RESOLUTION_INFO& res) const
+{
+  // Hades: the mode of the connector that res names carries the transport, at a rate that the
+  // display takes for native output (CDVModeMove)
+  const CDRMConnector* connector = m_DRM ? m_DRM->GetConnector() : nullptr;
+  const int index = res.strId.empty() ? -1 : std::atoi(res.strId.c_str());
+  if (!connector || index < 0 || index >= connector->GetModesCount())
+    return false;
+  const drmModeModeInfo& mode = *connector->GetModeForIndex(index);
+  return IsDVTransportMode(mode) && NativeDVTakesRate(ModeRate(mode));
+}
+
 CModeChangeHold::Change CWinSystemGbm::ModeChangeOf(const RESOLUTION_INFO& res) const
 {
   CModeChangeHold::Change change;
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.h b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.h
index 4667e4d..10e1384 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.h
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.h
@@ -305,6 +305,9 @@ protected:
   bool ModeAfterVideo(RESOLUTION_INFO& res) const;
   //! The mode of res differs from the mode selected (the one on the screen)
   bool OtherTiming(const RESOLUTION_INFO& res) const;
+  //! Hades: the mode of res carries the transport of native Dolby Vision, at a rate that the
+  //! display takes for it (CDVModeMove)
+  bool DVTransportModeOf(const RESOLUTION_INFO& res) const;
   //! A display that offers Dolby Vision was seen in this session (at init, or by a later look): it
   //! is looked at again with each video even while its EDID offers no Dolby Vision (an input
   //! setting, a failed read), so that what it offers again is seen.
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
index 72abdf3..2c69d55 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
@@ -236,6 +236,10 @@ bool CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::SetFullScreen(bool fullScreen,
   // signalling of a video that waited for this change goes out with its commit (STOP), and the
   // mode of a video that has not set up its output yet is dropped for this one (START)
   const bool heldEnd = EndModeHoldForModeChange();
+  // Hades: native Dolby Vision output that goes on into the mode of the video that takes it
+  // next: its next frame of the transport carries the change of mode, in one commit (CDVModeMove)
+  if (!heldEnd && DVModeMoves(res))
+    return true;
   // Hades: a video whose native Dolby Vision output ended waiting for this change of mode
   // (EndDVBridgeAfterVideo()): the ordinary output comes back in the new mode, in one commit
   // (FlipDVBridgePage()), with every backend. The other subsystems are told first, as the change
@@ -243,8 +247,9 @@ bool CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::SetFullScreen(bool fullScreen,
   // (nvidia-drm: the output off and on again), in the new mode.
   // If no restoration goes through at all, the mode of the video is selected again: Kodi keeps
   // its resolution when the change of it fails.
+  // (Hades: also one that native output moved into, and that no frame carried yet: CDVModeMove)
   const drmModeModeInfo* before = nullptr;
-  if (m_dvEndDeferred && DVModeChangeJoins(m_dvState, res))
+  if ((m_dvEndDeferred || m_dvMovePending) && DVModeChangeJoins(m_dvState, res))
   {
     OnLostDevice();
     m_displayLostSent = true;
@@ -470,6 +475,12 @@ void CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::PresentRender(bool rendered, bool videoLayer)
         AnnounceHeldModeChange(true);
         presented = FlipDVBridgePage(m_dvState, false, &flip);
         presentedAhead = presented && flip.ahead;
+        if (presented)
+        {
+          // (Hades: a mode that native output moved into went out with it: CDVModeMove)
+          m_dvMovePending = false;
+          m_dvHandOver = false;
+        }
         HeldModeChangeCommitted(presented, true);
         DVAheadEnd(presented, flip);
         if (presented && !m_dvSignalling)
@@ -598,6 +609,25 @@ void CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::PresentRender(bool rendered, bool videoLayer)
             m_dvRestoreRetry = now;
           }
         }
+        // Hades: the output kept, in the mode it moved into, for a video whose renderer is not
+        // configured yet (CDVModeMove): if none takes it in time, the ordinary output is restored
+        // in that mode, in one commit with it
+        else if (m_dvHandOver)
+        {
+          if (now >= m_dvHandOverUntil)
+          {
+            CLog::Log(LOGINFO,
+                      "DVBridge: no video took native Dolby Vision output within {} ms of the "
+                      "change of mode; the ordinary output is restored in that mode",
+                      CDVModeMove::WAIT_MS);
+            if (EndDVBridge())
+            {
+              SendDisplayReset();
+              return;
+            }
+            m_dvRestoreRetry = now;
+          }
+        }
         else if (now - m_dvRestoreRetry >= std::chrono::seconds(1))
         {
           m_dvRestoreRetry = now;
@@ -1896,6 +1926,27 @@ bool CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::SetVideoOutput(const VideoPicture* picture)
   // for the change of mode that follows (CModeChangeHold, STOP)
   if (!picture)
     HoldEndOfVideo();
+  // Hades: the renderer of the next video, configured while native output keeps the output
+  // (the end of the video before waits for a change of mode, or a move kept it for this video):
+  // where it draws natively in the same output surface, its frames go on in the transport, and
+  // nothing is restored (CDVModeMove::HandsOver())
+  if (const bool waiting = m_dvEndDeferred || m_dvHandOver;
+      picture && waiting &&
+      CDVModeMove::HandsOver(m_dvState.Captured(), true, m_dvRendererNative,
+                             VideoOutputKeepsSurface(picture), waiting))
+  {
+    m_dvEndDeferred = false;
+    m_dvHandOver = false;
+    // (the GUI is composed into the picture again: the renderer that went turned that off)
+    if (!m_guiCompositing || !m_compositeShader)
+    {
+      m_compositeShader.reset();
+      SetGuiCompositing(AVCOL_TRC_SMPTE2084);
+    }
+    CLog::Log(LOGINFO, "DVBridge: native Dolby Vision output goes on with the next video{}",
+              m_dvMovePending ? ", whose mode its next frame carries" : "");
+    return CWinSystemGbmEGLContext::SetVideoOutput(picture);
+  }
   // Restore with the current surface before EGL replaces its buffers. (Hades: not when a video has
   // stopped and its restoration waits for the change of mode that follows, while the window keeps
   // its surface: see EndDVBridgeAfterVideo().)
@@ -2297,6 +2348,56 @@ bool CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::HoldsModeForVideo(const RESOLUTION_INFO& res)
   return CModeChangeHold::StartHolds(video, ModeChangeOf(res));
 }
 
+bool CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::DVModeMoves(const RESOLUTION_INFO& res)
+{
+  // (the change of mode that VideoPlayer told of for a video that opens and goes out natively)
+  bool nativeOpens = false;
+  if (const int told = g_modeChangeResolution;
+      g_modeChangeOutput == static_cast<int>(DVBRIDGE::OpenedOutput::NATIVE_DV) && told >= 0)
+  {
+    const RESOLUTION_INFO& asked =
+        CDisplaySettings::GetInstance().GetResolutionInfo(static_cast<RESOLUTION>(told));
+    nativeOpens = asked.strId == res.strId && asked.iScreenWidth == res.iScreenWidth &&
+                  asked.iScreenHeight == res.iScreenHeight && asked.dwFlags == res.dwFlags;
+  }
+  CDVModeMove::State state;
+  state.captured = m_dvState.Captured();
+  state.transportLive = m_dvState.TransportLive();
+  state.disabled = NativeDVOutputDisabled();
+  state.joins = state.captured && DVModeChangeJoins(m_dvState, res);
+  state.transportMode = state.joins && DVTransportModeOf(res);
+  state.rendererNative = m_dvRendererNative;
+  state.endWaits = m_dvEndDeferred;
+  state.nativeOpens = nativeOpens;
+  if (!CDVModeMove::Moves(state))
+    return false;
+  // As HoldModeChange() chooses a mode: selected, and the next commit carries it (a modeset
+  // allowed); the other subsystems are told with that commit, the first frame of the next video
+  // that goes out natively (or the restoration of the ordinary output, if none does)
+  VideoSeen();
+  if (!m_DRM->SetMode(res))
+    return false;
+  m_DRM->SetVideoMode(res, nullptr);
+  m_modeAnnounce.Held();
+  m_dvMovePending = true;
+  // The end of the video before waited for this change: the output is kept for the video that
+  // opens, until its renderer is configured
+  if (m_dvEndDeferred.exchange(false))
+  {
+    m_dvHandOverUntil =
+        std::chrono::steady_clock::now() + std::chrono::milliseconds(CDVModeMove::WAIT_MS);
+    m_dvHandOver = true;
+  }
+  ResetOutputDepth();
+  CRenderSystemGLES::ResetRenderSystem(res.iWidth, res.iHeight);
+  CLog::Log(LOGINFO,
+            "DVBridge: native Dolby Vision output goes on into the mode {}x{} @ {:.3f} Hz of the "
+            "video that takes it{}: its next frame carries the change of mode, in one commit",
+            res.iScreenWidth, res.iScreenHeight, res.fRefreshRate,
+            m_dvHandOver ? " next" : "");
+  return true;
+}
+
 void CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::HoldEndOfVideo()
 {
   // (native Dolby Vision that ends waits its own way: EndDVBridgeAfterVideo())
@@ -2358,6 +2459,7 @@ bool CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::EndDVBridge(bool tellModeset)
   // the HDR metadata and the colorimetry while it waited.)
   if (m_dvEndDeferred.exchange(false))
     m_dvRestoreRequeue = true;
+  m_dvHandOver = false; // (Hades: and a move's wait for the next video, CDVModeMove)
   m_dvFrame = false;
   // Hades: no frame of native output is on the screen to be kept (KeepDVBridgeFrame())
   m_dvShown = {};
@@ -2395,9 +2497,15 @@ bool CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::EndDVBridge(bool tellModeset)
     // Hades: leaving the transport is a full modeset with every backend: told as a change of mode
     // (CHeldModeAnnouncement::Modeset()), unless the change of mode that it goes with tells of
     // itself, it is made again after a refusal, or the window goes
-    if (tellModeset && m_dvState.TransportLive() && !m_dvRestoreWithMode && !m_dvRestoreFailures)
+    const bool joinedByCaller = m_dvRestoreWithMode;
+    if (tellModeset && m_dvState.TransportLive() && !joinedByCaller && !m_dvRestoreFailures)
       m_modeAnnounce.Modeset();
-    if (!m_eglContext.TrySwapBuffers() || !FlipDVBridgePage(m_dvState, true))
+    // Hades: a mode that native output moved into, and that no frame of it carried (CDVModeMove),
+    // goes with this restoration, in one commit
+    m_dvRestoreWithMode = joinedByCaller || m_dvMovePending;
+    const bool restored = m_eglContext.TrySwapBuffers() && FlipDVBridgePage(m_dvState, true);
+    m_dvRestoreWithMode = joinedByCaller;
+    if (!restored)
     {
       // Retried once a second while the display refuses it (switched off): logged sparingly.
       if (++m_dvRestoreFailures <= 3 || m_dvRestoreFailures % 60 == 0)
@@ -2409,6 +2517,7 @@ bool CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::EndDVBridge(bool tellModeset)
     }
     m_dvRestoreFailures = 0;
     m_dvRestoreRequeue = false;
+    m_dvMovePending = false;
     // The next back buffer can still hold a packed transport frame: the ordinary output starts
     // from black, never from tunnel pixels. Kodi's GUI relies on the scissor test staying on
     // (only ResetRenderSystem() and ApplyStateBlock() turn it on again).
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.h b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.h
index a26e3be..ac787b6 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.h
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.h
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 #include "cores/VideoPlayer/Interface/TimingConstants.h"
 #include "DVAhead.h"
 #include "DVEngineSettings.h"
+#include "DVModeMove.h"
 #include "DVPathChoice.h"
 #include "DVPresentStall.h"
 #include "DVRepeatKeep.h"
@@ -90,7 +91,10 @@ public:
   void SetDVBridgeOverlays(bool visible) { m_dvOverlays = visible; }
   bool DVBridgeCaptured() const { return m_dvState.Captured(); }
   //! (not while the restoration waits for the change of mode after a video: no frame is there)
-  bool HasCaptureFramebuffer() const override { return m_dvState.Captured() && !m_dvEndDeferred; }
+  bool HasCaptureFramebuffer() const override
+  {
+    return m_dvState.Captured() && !m_dvEndDeferred && !m_dvHandOver;
+  }
   unsigned int GetCaptureFramebuffer(int& width, int& height) override;
   //! Route the HDR overlays that Kodi draws right after the video into the Dolby Vision PQ
   //! picture. Returns false (nothing changed) when there is no such picture this frame.
@@ -302,6 +306,14 @@ private:
   //! EndDVBridgeAfterVideo(): the restoration waits for the change of mode, until then
   std::atomic<bool> m_dvEndDeferred{false};
   std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point m_dvEndDeferredUntil{};
+  //! Hades: native output goes on into the mode of the video that takes it next (CDVModeMove):
+  //! res is selected, and the next commit carries it. True when that is done.
+  bool DVModeMoves(const RESOLUTION_INFO& res);
+  //! ... the mode that it moved into is not committed yet
+  bool m_dvMovePending = false;
+  //! ... the output is kept for a video whose renderer is not configured yet, until then
+  std::atomic<bool> m_dvHandOver{false};
+  std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point m_dvHandOverUntil{};
   //! Hades: a change of mode for the video that opens (VideoPlayer) is held for the output of that
   //! video (CModeChangeHold, START): it is the one that VideoPlayer told of, and res is that change
   bool HoldsModeForVideo(const RESOLUTION_INFO& res);
